smart-object-select bundles model files derived from the following third-party model.

Model: yolo11n-seg
Source: https://huggingface.co/mobilint/YOLO11n-seg
  (unmodified fp32 ONNX export of YOLO11n-seg, published by mobilint as the
  pre-quantization input to their NPU compilation pipeline; the `.mxq` NPU-specific
  files in that repository are NOT used by this application)
Original model: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics (YOLO11n-seg, COCO-pretrained,
  80-class instance segmentation)
  Ultralytics YOLO11 weights and code are licensed under the GNU Affero General Public
  License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0) (https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/blob/main/LICENSE).

License:
  This model (both the original Ultralytics YOLO11n-seg weights and the mobilint ONNX
  export republishing them, which itself declares `license: agpl-3.0` in its Hugging
  Face repository card metadata) is licensed under AGPL-3.0. A copy of the AGPL-3.0
  license text is included at the repository root (`LICENSE`); this repository (this
  smart-object-select project) is published as AGPL-3.0 in full to satisfy this
  requirement (source-available on GitHub, including when accessed over a network,
  per AGPL-3.0 Section 13). This decision was confirmed with the repository owner
  (issue #45 Decision Log #4, issue #49).

  Unlike MobileSAM (Apache-2.0, public/models/mobile-sam/NOTICE) and EdgeSAM (S-Lab
  License 1.0 / non-commercial, public/models/edge-sam/NOTICE), YOLO11n-seg's AGPL-3.0
  is a copyleft (not permissive, not non-commercial-only) license: commercial use is
  allowed, but any distribution (including network use, i.e. running this app as a
  service) requires making the complete corresponding source code available under
  AGPL-3.0. This repository being fully public on GitHub satisfies that requirement.

Files included:
  - yolo11n-seg.onnx (fp32 ONNX export; input tensor `input` [batch, 3, 640, 640],
    output tensors of shape [1, 116, 8400] (4 box + 80 COCO class scores + 32 mask
    coefficients per detection candidate) and [1, 32, 160, 160] (mask prototypes) —
    this app's decoder (src/lib/modelLab/yolo11nSeg/postprocess.ts) reads outputs by
    shape, not by name, since the exact output tensor names differ slightly from the
    "vanilla" Ultralytics `yolo export format=onnx` naming (`output0`/`output1`) while
    the numerical content and shapes are identical).

Changes made:
  - No modification was made to the file contents. The file was copied verbatim from
    the upstream Hugging Face repository into public/models/yolo11n-seg/ so that
    smart-object-select can serve the model from its own origin instead of fetching it
    from the Hugging Face Hub at runtime.

Scope limitation (see issue #49, parent #45):
  - This model is a closed-set detector trained only on the 80 COCO classes. It cannot
    detect or segment arbitrary objects outside that class set. This limitation is
    surfaced in the Model Lab UI (src/pages/ModelLabPage.tsx) whenever YOLO11n-seg is
    the selected model.
